        </para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>

    <bridgehead renderas="sect3">Dependências do &quot;Pango&quot;</bridgehead>

    <bridgehead renderas="sect4">Exigidas</bridgehead>
    <para role="required">
      <xref linkend="fontconfig"/> (precisa ser construído com <xref
linkend="freetype2"/> usando <xref linkend="harfbuzz"/>), <xref
linkend="fribidi"/> e <xref linkend="glib2"/> (GObject Introspection exigido
para GNOME)
    </para>

    <bridgehead renderas="sect4">Recomendadas</bridgehead>
    <para role="recommended">
      <xref linkend="cairo"/> (construído depois de <xref linkend="harfbuzz"/>) e
<xref linkend="xorg7-lib"/>
    </para>

    <bridgehead renderas="sect4">Opcionais</bridgehead>
    <para role="optional">
  
  
      <!--<xref linkend="gtk-doc"/>
,-->
<!--<xref linkend="sysprof"/>
,-->
<xref linkend="gi-docgen"/> (para gerar documentação), <ulink
url="https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/gnu/help2man">help2man</ulink>, <ulink
url="https://linux.thai.net/projects/libthai">libthai</ulink> e <ulink
url="&sysprof-url;">sysprof</ulink>
    </para>

  </sect2>

  <sect2 role="installation">
    <title>Instalação do Pango</title>

    <para>
      Instale o &quot;<application>Pango</application>&quot; executando os
seguintes comandos:
    </para>

<screen><userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=/usr            \
            --buildtype=release      \
            --wrap-mode=nofallback   \
            -D introspection=enabled \
            ..                       &amp;&amp;
ninja</userinput></screen>

    <para>
      Se você tiver <xref linkend='gi-docgen'/> instalado e desejar construir a
documentação da API para esse pacote, emita:
    </para>

<screen remap='doc'><userinput>sed "/docs_dir =/s@\$@ / 'pango-&pango-version;'@" -i ../docs/meson.build &amp;&amp;
meson configure -D documentation=true                            &amp;&amp;
ninja</userinput></screen>

    <para>
      <!-- Related discussion:
           https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3518
           Setting LD_LIBRARY_PATH to a Glib build at revision b180a8ec7032
           makes the test pass.  -->
Para testar os resultados, emita: <command>ninja test</command>. Um teste
chamado testboundaries_ucd é conhecido por falhar porque espera suporte
Unicode 16.0 originário da Glib 2.83 ou mais recente.
    </para>

    <para>
      Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem
class="username">root</systemitem>&quot;:
    </para>

<!--
This requires the external help2man program to generate pango-view.1.  The version
from lsb_release is insufficient.  I'm not sure if the command below is needed
or not if the newer help2man is present. - Bruce

install -vm 644 ../utils/pango-view.1.in /usr/share/man/man1/pango-view.1</userinput></screen>
-->
<screen role="root"><userinput>ninja install</userinput></screen>



  </sect2>

